bhyve/arm64: the PSCI node is also compatible with arm,psci-0.2

PSCI 1.0 keeps the 0.2 function IDs and the binding has a 1.0 node list
"arm,psci-0.2" as well for clients that only know that one.  EDK2's
ArmVirt reset library is one: without it the firmware stops at an
assertion in ResetSystemRuntimeDxe.

--- a/usr.sbin/bhyve/aarch64/fdt.c
+++ b/usr.sbin/bhyve/aarch64/fdt.c
@@ -154,7 +154,9 @@
 	add_cpus(fdt, ncpu);
 
 	fdt_begin_node(fdt, "psci");
-	fdt_property_string(fdt, "compatible", "arm,psci-1.0");
+#define	PSCI_COMPAT	"arm,psci-1.0\0arm,psci-0.2"
+	fdt_property(fdt, "compatible", PSCI_COMPAT, sizeof(PSCI_COMPAT));
+#undef PSCI_COMPAT
 	fdt_property_string(fdt, "method", "hvc");
 	fdt_end_node(fdt);
 
